    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Medication: continued without change, Furosemide 20 mg oral tablet, one tablet by mouth as needed for a weight gain of more than 1 kg in a day or 2 kg in a week [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Empagliflozin 10 mg oral tablet, one tablet by mouth daily [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Spironolactone 25 mg oral tablet, one-half tablet (12.5 mg) by mouth daily [S]</item><item>Goal: Reach euvolemia with no ankle edema and a stable dry weight within three months. Outcome by 1905-06-29: Dry weight 56 kg; furosemide changed to as-needed use [S]</item><item>Goal: Improve the KCCQ-12 overall summary score by at least 15 points by the three-month review. Outcome by 1905-06-29: KCCQ-12 rose from 52 to 70 [S]</item><item>Goal: Lower blood pressure below 130/80 by the six-month review without orthostatic symptoms. Outcome by 1905-09-28: Blood pressure 126/72; no dizziness on standing [S]</item><item>Goal: Resume a full speaking and travel schedule by the six-month review. Outcome by 1905-09-28: Back to lecturing twice a month with a travel weight plan [S]</item><item>Continue the care plan agreed on 1905-03-16 [S]</item><item>Scheduled episode complete. Continue routine follow-up [S]</item></list></text>

